### Phase 2 — ZODB, Persistence, ACID Transactions & Acquisition
### Click "Send Request" (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Start server first: .\run.bat

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8080

### 1. Health Check (shows ZODB store & count in Data.fs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api-health
Accept: application/json

### 2. List Active Employees from ZODB OOBTree
GET {{baseUrl}}/api-employees
Accept: application/json

### 3. Get Single Employee + Acquisition Demo (company_name inherited from EmployeeFolder)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api-employees/EMP-0001
Accept: application/json

### 4. Create New Employee in ZODB (auto-committed to var/Data.fs, survives server restart!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api-employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "empCode": "EMP-0004",
  "nameEn": "Daiki Takahashi",
  "nameJa": "高橋 大樹",
  "departmentEn": "Engineering",
  "departmentJa": "開発部",
  "role": "Backend Engineer",
  "email": "d.takahashi@example.co.jp",
  "skills": ["Java", "Spring Boot", "MySQL"]
}

### 5. Duplicate Employee Error (409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api-employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "empCode": "EMP-0004",
  "nameEn": "Daiki Takahashi",
  "nameJa": "高橋 大樹",
  "departmentEn": "Engineering",
  "departmentJa": "開発部",
  "role": "Backend Engineer",
  "email": "d.takahashi@example.co.jp"
}

### 6. ACID Transaction Rollback Demo (returns 500 and does NOT save EMP-9999 to ZODB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api-employees?simulateError=true
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "empCode": "EMP-9999",
  "nameEn": "Rollback Test",
  "nameJa": "ロールバックテスト",
  "departmentEn": "QA",
  "departmentJa": "品質保証部",
  "role": "Tester",
  "email": "rollback@example.co.jp"
}

### 7. Verify EMP-9999 was Rolled Back (expect 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api-employees/EMP-9999
Accept: application/json

### 8. PersistentList Mutation Demo (add skill to EMP-0004 and persist in ZODB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api-employees/EMP-0004/skills
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "skill": "Zope 5"
}

### 9. Soft Delete Employee (sets deletedFlg = true in ZODB)
### Note: Zope treats DELETE/PUT on plain folder paths as WebDAV by default.
### Prefixing the view with "@@" bypasses WebDAV and routes straight to BrowserView!
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/@@api-employees/EMP-0004
Accept: application/json

### 10. List Including Soft-Deleted Employees (?includeDeleted=true)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api-employees?includeDeleted=true
Accept: application/json
